  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A person can throw a ball upto a maximum range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. How high above the ground he can throw the same ball?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pCnYp",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sBrYh",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vdtrH",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sKSSh",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Horizontal range is maximum if the angle of projection is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>If the&nbsp;ball is thrown vertically upward, then the ball will attain the maximum height from the ground as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
